Agreed.  There is obviously a good deal of nice content to keep you busy 
(if you believe the good player reviews, which seem to outnumber the bad 
player reviews more and more each day).  I'd rather plonk down 30 bucks 
on a game I know I'll be able to at least get some enjoyment out of, 
than spend that or more on something that will bore me and end up on a 
shelf collecting dust.  Hell, just the fact that the construction kit 
and additions are already coming out should basically guarantee I get 
many hours out of the game, and gives me hope that any of the things 
that people find negative (and might irritate me) can be fixed with some 
clever mods.

I actually ordered my copy from gogamer today, it was about the same 
price as Amazon, so it looks like I'll be touring the wastelands by 
year's end - if I can find any time to actually play the damn thing!  heh.

